      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<ul><li>Betta pugnax complex</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern</li><li>Mouthbrooder type betta</li><li>Temperament: territorial; can be kept in pairs with adequate space</li><li>Max size: 4+ inches (over 10 cm)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<p>Originates from Sumatra, Indonesia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<p>The natural habitat consists of calm, blackwater streams with overhanging plants and vegetation.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<p>These bettas can get very big, so it is recommended to house them in tanks of 10 gallons or larger.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: 60 - 200 (kept in soft water with low TDS, but they are more tolerant of water conditions)</li><li>pH: 6.5 - 7.5</li><li>Temperature: 75-85 °F (24-29 °C); much better coloration at warmer temperatures above 78 °F (26 °C)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<p>Territorial. They can be maintained in a pair or a group, given adequate space.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-anabatoides-wild-type-bettas-1",
      "html": "<p>Males are generally larger, with more iridescence on the cheek plates.</p>"
    },
